istributed."},"3-g":{"markScheme":["Apply heading styles/levels. Up to 2 marks.","Generate/update the table of contents from those headings. Up to 2 marks."],"responseType":"prose","profile":"Productivity Tools","prompt":"Explain how headings can be used to create an automatic table of contents."},"3-h":{"markScheme":["Any two of automatic save, backup copy, password/edit restriction. Up to 4 marks."],"responseType":"prose","profile":"Productivity Tools","prompt":"State TWO methods of protecting an important document from accidental loss or unauthorised editing."},"4-a":{"markScheme":["Input: timeScore, attendance, fitness. 1 mark.","Process: calculate the score and compare with the threshold. 1 mark.","Output: ACCEPT or REVIEW. 1 mark."],"responseType":"ipo","profile":"Problem-Solving and Programming","prompt":"Construct an IPO chart for the qualification score problem using the three inputs timeScore, attendance, fitness."},"4-b":{"markScheme":["Any two of finite, precise, unambiguous, clear flow of control, terminates. 2 marks.","One suitable explanation. 2 marks."],"responseType":"prose","profile":"Problem-Solving and Programming","prompt":"State TWO characteristics of a good algorithm and explain ONE of them."},"4-c":{"markScheme":["Read/input all three values. 2 marks.","Calculate SCORE using all three values. 2 marks.","Correct IF condition using threshold. 1 mark.","Display ACCEPT on true branch. 1 mark.","ELSE/otherwise branch. 1 mark.","Display REVIEW on false branch. 1 mark."],"responseType":"pseudocode","profile":"Problem-Solving and Programming","prompt":"Write language-neutral pseudocode that reads timeScore, attendance, fitness, calculates a SCORE using all three values, and displays ACCEPT when SCORE is at least 75, otherwise REVIEW."},"4-d":{"markScheme":["Use selected test data. 1 mark.","Record changing values/identifiers step by step. 1 mark.","Follow decision/control flow. 1 mark.","Compare actual result with expected result or identify logic errors. 1 mark."],"responseType":"prose","profile":"Problem-Solving and Programming","prompt":"Explain how a trace table or dry run could be used to test the algorithm."},"4-e":{"markScheme":["Syntax error breaks language rules and may prevent successful translation/execution. 1–2 marks.","Logic error allows execution but produces an incorrect result. 1–2 marks."],"responseType":"prose","profile":"Problem-Solving and Programming","prompt":"Distinguish between a syntax error and a logic error."},"4-f":{"markScheme":["Any three of meaningful variable names, useful comments, indentation and effective whitespace. 1 mark each."],"responseType":"prose","profile":"Problem-Solving and Programming","prompt":"State THREE features of good internal program documentation."}}'::jsonb;
